From bec149d3d00401c20c5115fed81d61a0fbb96118 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 05:36:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] =?UTF-8?q?feat(blueprints):=20BP1670=20=E2=80=94=20re?=
 =?UTF-8?q?fuse=20a=20Get/SetVariable=20that=20targets=20nothing?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An unresolvable VariableId missed both index lookups, returned -1, and the
emitter wrote `s.__var_-1 = __t0;` — not a C# identifier. The blueprint
compile reported NO diagnostic; the solution build then failed with a CS error
pointing at a generated file, naming neither the graph nor the node.

Pre-existing, but BP-57 makes it reachable: deleting a local leaves every
Get/Set that targeted it dangling, and BP-225 established that delete/rename
maintenance is exactly where this lands. The rail comes before the gesture.

Both halves, as the design allows: the Stage-2 rail is the diagnostic and
names the node; VarFieldName now throws on a negative index, which is the
assertion that the rail is complete. The throw is deliberately narrower than
"out of range" — a positive-but-oversized index is BP-226's index-space
ambiguity and is not touched here.

Scope measured before it was built, and the measurement corrected the premise:
the ~60 literal "state"/"rally" references in the shipped corpus are on
GetShared/SetShared, a different node kind whose VariableId is a name-keyed
slot resolved at runtime and never passed to FindVariableIndex. Across the 58
shipped assets all 103 Get/SetVariable references resolve (46 Variables, 57
WorkingState, 0 Parameters, 0 dangling), so this refuses nothing that ships.
A rail generalised to "any node with a VariableId" would have rejected six.

Also §4: the BP-220 block documenting WithNodesAndLinks had been orphaned onto
LocalVariables when Batch 37 inserted the field between the comment and its
method, leaving LocalVariables with two summaries and the method with none.
Moved back, and its own summary updated from A1 to A3.

